1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,910
Every AI image tool works the same way:

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:04,290
you type a prompt,

3
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:05,410
and you pray.

4
00:00:05,870 --> 00:00:08,050
This one lets you build the scene first,

5
00:00:08,110 --> 00:00:09,080
like a film set,

6
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:10,800
and only then generate.

7
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:12,610
It's called ArtCraft.

8
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,800
It's free, open source,

9
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:16,900
and it just picked up over three thousand

10
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:18,880
GitHub stars in a single day.

11
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,150
Its makers call it the IDE for artists:

12
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:25,360
one app where you compose in 2D and stage

13
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:26,570
scenes in 3D.

14
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:28,160
Drop in a room,

15
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:30,260
place your actors, and pose them like

16
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:30,910
mannequins.

17
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:33,620
Then put the camera exactly where you want

18
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,080
it, and frame the shot.

19
00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:38,020
Turn any picture into a 3D object you can

20
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:40,860
rotate, and kitbash whole sets from asset

21
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:41,500
kits.

22
00:00:41,850 --> 00:00:43,740
Then you generate, and your posed

23
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:45,500
mannequins guide where the characters

24
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:46,080
stand.

25
00:00:46,530 --> 00:00:48,550
Keep the same room for every shot,

26
00:00:48,610 --> 00:00:50,730
so a whole sequence stays consistent.

27
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:52,720
Want a quick idea instead?

28
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:55,010
Type a prompt, edit with a mask,

29
00:00:55,090 --> 00:00:56,970
or turn a still into video.

30
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,420
It plugs into a long list of models,

31
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:02,800
including Midjourney, Sora, Grok and World

32
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:04,270
Labs' 3D worlds.

33
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:05,750
The app is free.

34
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:08,180
Generating isn't: bring your own

35
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:10,400
subscriptions, or buy credits,

36
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:12,820
from 8 dollars a month billed yearly.

37
00:01:13,330 --> 00:01:15,090
It runs on Windows and Mac,

38
00:01:15,340 --> 00:01:17,330
and on Linux if you build it yourself.

39
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:19,560
Stop prompting and praying.

40
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:20,980
Start directing.

41
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,680
That's today's tool.

42
00:01:23,010 --> 00:01:25,590
Subscribe, there's a new one every day.
